Import from `@/components/ui/agents-builder`. A complete agent workspace (chat, inbox, schedules, integrations, skills, and an agent view with a live run) that renders only what `data` holds: the block owns navigation between its views, the connect dialog, and scripted playback; the host owns the data, routing, OAuth, persistence, and every action it reports.

It fills its parent, so give the parent a bounded height:
```tsx
'use client';
import { AGENTS_BUILDER_DEMO, AgentsBuilder, type AgentsBuilderData } from '@/components/ui/agents-builder';

// The type is large: spread the demo and replace what you have.
const data: AgentsBuilderData = {
  ...AGENTS_BUILDER_DEMO,
  workspace: { name: 'Acme', appName: 'Acme' },
  agents: [{ id: 'revenue-analyst', name: 'Revenue Analyst', running: true }],
};

<div className="h-dvh">
  <AgentsBuilder
    data={data}
    onAuthorizeIntegration={(integration) => startOAuth(integration.id)}
    onConnectIntegration={(integration, toolIds) => saveConnection(integration.id, toolIds)}
    onAction={(action) => {
      if (action.type === 'open-agent') router.push(`/agents/${action.agentId}`);
    }}
  />
</div>
```
`data` holds `workspace` (`{ name, appName }`), `models`, `integrations` (`{ id, name, description, vendor, authDomain, connected, tools: { id, name, access: 'read' | 'write' }[] }`), `categories`, `featuredIntegrationIds`, `agents` (`{ id, name, running? }`), `inbox`, `schedules`, `clock`, `skills`, `starterPacks`, `recommendations`, `fallbackReply`, `followUpReply`, `agent` (the agent view's blueprint), `run`, `heroHighlights`, and `usage: { percent }`.

Chat is scripted and sends nothing to the host: a recommendation plays its `reply`, a first typed message plays `fallbackReply`, and later ones play `followUpReply`. For a chat answered by a live model, build it from the `ai` item's transcript and composer instead.

- `view` / `defaultView` / `onViewChange(view)`: `'chat' | 'inbox' | 'schedules' | 'integrations' | 'skills' | 'agent'`, default `'chat'`.
- `onAuthorizeIntegration(integration) => Promise<void>` runs the connect dialog's sign-in step: resolve to move on to choosing tools, reject to go back. Without it the dialog waits a moment and moves on.
- `onConnectIntegration(integration, toolIds: string[]) => void | Promise<void>` saves the connection; reject to keep the dialog open. Once it resolves the integration shows as connected (tracked locally, seeded from each `connected` flag).
- `onAction(action)` gets every control the block doesn't own: `navigate { target: 'usage' | 'settings' | 'more-agents' }`, `open-agent { agentId }` (`data.agent.id` opens the built-in view instead), `new-agent`, `search { query }`, `workspace-menu { item: 'organization' | 'profile' | 'support' | 'whats-new' | 'log-out' }`, `workspace-mode { mode: 'agents' | 'workbench' }`, `chat-history`, `attach-file { surface: 'chat' | 'run' }`, `send-follow-up { surface: 'run', text }`, `stop-run`, `approve-run { agentId, approved }`, `send-reply { threadId, text, drafted }`, `approve-thread-action { threadId }`, `new-schedule`, `toggle-schedule { scheduleId, active }`, `run-schedule { scheduleId }`, `share-agent` / `edit-instructions` / `set-identity { agentId }`, `request-app`, `manage-integration { integrationId }`, `create-skill`, `browse-skill-library`, `add-starter-pack { packId }`, `open-skill { skillId }`, `create-agent { draft: { name, schedule, integrationIds, steps } }`.
- `theme` / `onThemeChange` (`'light' | 'dark' | 'system'`) only drive the menu's appearance switch; apply the theme yourself.
- `defaultSidebarCollapsed`, `framed` (a rounded window on a canvas), `autoplayRun` (default true; false opens the run settled), `className`.
